{"id": "EUVD-2026-86766", "enisaUuid": "75758dbd-6387-3d0c-b0f1-6677c47014e3", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\naccel: ethosu: Ensure SRAM size is 0 on mapping failure\n\nOn a mapping failure of the SRAM, the SRAM size is left as non-zero. The\nprobe will succeed as the error return is not checked since having SRAM is\nnot a hard requirement. The non-zero size allows jobs to access SRAM which\nis left pointing to physical base address 0x0.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:22:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:10:38", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e5576641b79ecd36acaf91fec4a5333b1ad19c57", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f5376d7e0fb703876199d3b6f9f97e128fa2f8a4"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97912", "GHSA-3c99-6rw9-787g"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "6a8f7241-3698-3819-837b-8aa6db8ae674", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5a5e9c0228e613f0ef2a58b9782d7c0ea8f1e58b <e5576641b79ecd36acaf91fec4a5333b1ad19c57"}, {"id": "6b4c65d8-cd5d-3e57-b746-3988fd72baa8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "761178e6-4696-31a6-ac61-e807f592e673", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "bf16c8e7-fd40-3f5d-b254-58cb5717889f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5a5e9c0228e613f0ef2a58b9782d7c0ea8f1e58b <f5376d7e0fb703876199d3b6f9f97e128fa2f8a4"}, {"id": "cf2ccf5d-a384-3cfa-9491-ca1c810c879e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "e431c6a5-19e9-3c08-9bd6-63d27e86da6e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.19"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8ade7013-9f02-3c31-bf11-cba733803e9b", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}